{"id": "xfalkland", "name": "Falkland Islands: Saunders Island and surrounding sea", "short": "Falklands", "place": "Falkland Islands", "lat": -51.3, "lon": -60.2, "side": "r", "cont": "South America", "country": "Falkland Is.", "kind": "Coast & ocean", "park": true, "blurb": "Tussac shores, penguin colonies and the cold sea that feeds seabirds and seals.", "tip": {"id": "munida", "title": "Thin out the lobster krill", "text": "Lobster krill feed squid and penguins. Set Lobster krill to -100% and watch the squid, the penguins, then the seals and scavengers above them."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Falkland Islands", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Falkland_Islands"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Tussac grass", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tussac_grass"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Black-browed albatross", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black-browed_albatross"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Striated caracara", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Striated_caracara"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: South American sea lion", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_American_sea_lion"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Southern rockhopper penguin", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southern_rockhopper_penguin"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Falkland Islands", "icon": "seal", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "sun", "sp": "sunlight", "xh": 0.1, "desc": "Long summer days power the tussac, shrubs, kelp and plankton that the whole web is built on."}, {"id": "current", "sp": "cold, nutrient-rich current", "xh": 0.35}, {"id": "soil", "sp": "wet coastal ground", "xh": 0.6}, {"id": "decomp", "sp": "decomposer community", "xh": 0.9, "name": "Bacteria and fungi", "desc": "Break down dead plants, kelp, carcasses and droppings, returning nutrients to the soil and water."}, {"id": "tussac", "sp": "poa flabellata", "xh": 0.08}, {"id": "diddle", "sp": "empetrum rubrum", "xh": 0.3, "desc": "A low dwarf shrub of the treeless Falklands heath. It bears berries and was among the most recorded plants near this site."}, {"id": "kelp", "sp": "macrocystis pyrifera", "xh": 0.55, "desc": "Large brown seaweed forming kelp beds in the cold coastal water around the islands.", "no": ["badge"]}, {"id": "phyto", "sp": "thalassiosira", "xh": 0.8}, {"id": "munida", "sp": "munida gregaria", "xh": 0.1}, {"id": "kelpgoose", "sp": "chloephaga hybrida", "xh": 0.28}, {"id": "sheep", "sp": "ovis aries", "xh": 0.46, "name": "Sheep", "desc": "Introduced livestock; virtually all land on the islands is used as sheep pasture, where they graze native grasses."}, {"id": "thrush", "sp": "turdus falcklandii", "xh": 0.66, "desc": "A common songbird that nests in tussac on the Falklands. It feeds on invertebrates and berries."}, {"id": "squid", "sp": "doryteuthis gahi", "xh": 0.06}, {"id": "rockhopper", "sp": "eudyptes chrysocome", "xh": 0.2}, {"id": "magellanic", "sp": "spheniscus magellanicus", "xh": 0.34, "desc": "A burrowing penguin breeding on the islands and one of the most recorded birds near this site. It eats fish, squid and crustaceans.", "ic": "meadowlark"}, {"id": "albatross", "sp": "thalassarche melanophris", "xh": 0.48}, {"id": "elephant", "sp": "mirounga leonina", "xh": 0.62, "desc": "Breeds on Falkland beaches; a large seal that dives for squid and fish."}, {"id": "skua", "sp": "stercorarius antarcticus", "xh": 0.76}, {"id": "petrel", "sp": "macronectes giganteus", "xh": 0.88, "desc": "A large scavenging seabird that feeds on carrion from seals and penguins and also preys on penguin chicks."}, {"id": "caracara", "sp": "phalcoboenus australis", "xh": 0.95}, {"id": "sealion", "sp": "otaria byronia", "xh": 0.3, "tl": 4, "desc": "Eats fish, squid and crustaceans and also hunts penguins. The Falklands population is declining."},